11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "767 reaches 1635 only along routes whose slowest hop is ~27350 time units (notably the terminal 302->1635 contact at t=52915, long after any upstream contact). Under the required 600-unit relay constraint, 767's temporal horizon collapses to 4 nodes and never touches 1635 or any of its in-neighbours; even a 3000-unit allowance fails. The static path and the nodes' ordinary activity levels therefore reflect an ignore-time connection, not a genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion:** The connection exists only when the 600-unit gap constraint is relaxed.\n\n- With `max_wait=600`, only 4 nodes are reachable from 767 at all, and 1635 is not among them (step_01), nor are any of 1635's in-neighbours 302/106/133 (steps 11\u201313).\n- A time-respecting route does exist ignoring the gap limit, but its hop waits are 611 and **27350** time units (step_03) \u2014 the final hop 302\u21921635 at t=52915 follows the previous contact by ~7.6 hours of graph time. All alternative routes (step_05) share the same late 302\u21921635 edge at 52915, and every route's slowest hop far exceeds 600.\n- Even loosening the constraint 5\u00d7 to `max_wait=3000` leaves 1635 unreached (step_08).\n- Confounder controls: both endpoints are low-degree (7 events, 7 distinct partners each \u2014 not popularity artefacts, step_04); the graph is large and busy (8217 events, 1967 active nodes, step_02) so failure isn't from sparse data overall; the static neighbourhood of 767 is a small closed cluster not containing 1635 (step_14); and 767/1635 activity is spread thinly across the whole window rather than concentrated near a shared burst (step_15).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_049448d4\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [767, 1635, 722, 302],\n  \"window\": [20674, 59073],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"767 reaches 1635 only along routes whose slowest hop is ~27350 time units (notably the terminal 302->1635 contact at t=52915, long after any upstream contact). Under the required 600-unit relay constraint, 767's temporal horizon collapses to 4 nodes and never touches 1635 or any of its in-neighbours; even a 3000-unit allowance fails. The static path and the nodes' ordinary activity levels therefore reflect an ignore-time connection, not a genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40466, "total_output_tokens": 3270, "total_tokens": 43736, "total_latency_ms": 52351, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}